# HR360 — Frontend API Integration Document

**Document ID:** HR360-FE-004
**Version:** 1.0
**Status:** Draft for Review
**Date:** 20 September 2026
**Prepared By:** Nida Khan

## 1. Purpose

This document defines how the React frontend will communicate with the existing HR360 Node.js/Express REST APIs.

## 2. Integration Architecture

```text
React Component
      |
      v
Frontend Service
      |
      v
API Client
      |
      v
HTTP Request
      |
      v
Express REST API
      |
      v
PostgreSQL
```

## 3. API Base URL

Development:

```env
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
```

The API URL shall be configurable through the frontend environment.

## 4. API Service Structure

```text
services/
├── api.js
├── employeeService.js
├── departmentService.js
├── attendanceService.js
├── leaveService.js
├── performanceService.js
├── trainingService.js
├── recruitmentService.js
└── analyticsService.js
```

## 5. API Modules

| Module            | Endpoint                   |
| ----------------- | -------------------------- |
| Employees         | `/api/employees`           |
| Departments       | `/api/departments`         |
| Job Roles         | `/api/job-roles`           |
| Work Statuses     | `/api/work-statuses`       |
| Attendance        | `/api/attendance`          |
| Leave Types       | `/api/leave-types`         |
| Leave Requests    | `/api/leave-requests`      |
| Performance       | `/api/performance-reviews` |
| PIP               | `/api/pips`                |
| Training Programs | `/api/training-programs`   |
| Employee Training | `/api/employee-training`   |
| Candidates        | `/api/candidates`          |
| Applications      | `/api/job-applications`    |
| Interviews        | `/api/interviews`          |
| Job Offers        | `/api/job-offers`          |
| Analytics         | `/api/analytics`           |

## 6. Request Flow

```text
User Action
   ↓
React Component
   ↓
Service Function
   ↓
API Request
   ↓
Backend
   ↓
Database
   ↓
JSON Response
   ↓
React State
   ↓
UI Refresh
```

## 7. HTTP Methods

The frontend shall use standard REST methods:

```text
GET     Retrieve
POST    Create
PUT/PATCH Update
DELETE  Delete where supported
```

## 8. Response Handling

Successful responses shall update the appropriate React state.

Failed responses shall:

* Display a user-friendly message
* Preserve the current UI where possible
* Allow retry
* Avoid exposing technical details

## 9. Loading State

Each API-driven page shall provide a loading state while waiting for a response.

## 10. Validation

Frontend validation shall improve user experience.

Backend validation remains authoritative.

## 11. Employee Active Status

The employee service shall retrieve the backend-calculated:

```text
department_active_status
```

The frontend shall display the value without recreating the department-specific business logic.

## 12. Analytics Integration

Analytics services shall consume:

```text
/api/analytics/overview
/api/analytics/departments
/api/analytics/attendance
/api/analytics/leave
/api/analytics/performance
/api/analytics/training
/api/analytics/recruitment
```

## 13. Security

The frontend shall never contain:

* PostgreSQL credentials
* Backend database passwords
* Private API secrets

Only frontend-safe environment variables may be exposed through Vite.

## 14. Planned Integration

The following remains planned:

```text
Accepted Job Offer
        ↓
Employee Creation
```

The frontend shall not represent this as implemented until the backend capability exists.

## 15. Testing

API integration shall be tested for:

* Successful GET
* Successful POST
* Successful UPDATE
* Validation errors
* Invalid IDs
* Server errors
* Empty responses
* Database-related failures

